S|       1       EXT. FOOTBALL PITCH - BAN CHONG, THAILAND - DAY          1           
O|
Y|               DAY 1 - Saturday June 23                                             
O|
N|               A thick mist hangs over Nang Non mountain, a curtain of dark         
N,G|               green tropical vegetation. DOWN TO FIND a football pitch,            
N|               where the under-15 team of local club the Wild Boars are             
N|               having a kick-around for practice, under the eye of their            
N,I|               young COACH, 25.                                                     
O|
N,I|               The tallest boy in the team, gangling LEK, has the ball at           
N,I|               his feet and is racing for the goal. The smallest boy in the         
N,I|               team, his friend little CHAI, is on his heels, trying to             
N|               tackle him, weaving in and out, constantly out-played.               
N,I|               ARM, the team captain, urges Chai on.                                
O|
C|                                   ARM                                              
U|                         Go Chai! Go Chai!                                          
O|
N,I|               PREM, the team clown, can’t stop laughing at the sight of            
N|               little Chai trying to tackle big Lek. Lek slams the ball             
N|               between the goal posts. He does a victory dance like his             
N|               hero, football star Ronaldo.                                         
N|               Coach blows his whistle. The boys race to the side of the            
N|               pitch, where there’s a cart selling grilled pork skewers.            
N|               They’re hungry, and they jostle to get the food.                     
O|
C|                                   CHAI                                             
U|                         Here comes Messi, greatest player                          
U|                         in the world!                                              
O|
N|               He clenches his fists and does the Messi shoulder shake. Prem        
N|               finds this hilarious.                                                
O|
C|                                   PREM                                             
U|                         Messi! My hero! Let me touch your                          
U|                         golden boots!                                              
N|               Arm comes up to Prem, holding a bag -                                
O|
C|                                   ARM                                              
U|                         Hey, birthday boy! Today’s your                            
U|                         day!                                                       
O|
C|                                   PREM                                             
U|                         You’re all invited to my party!                            
O|
C|                                   ARM                                              
U|                         But first -                                                
O|
O|
O|                 THIRTEEN LIVES | FULL PINK REVISIONS | 19.3.21 Pg 2.
O|
N|               He takes a flashlight from his bag and shines it in Prem’s           
N|               face.                                                                
C|                                   ARM                                              
U|                         Guess where we’re going?                                   
O|
N|               He shines the flashlight round the other boys. They let out a        
N|               cheer and race for their bikes. Lek stays back with Coach.           
O|
C|                                   LEK                                              
U|                         My dad’s cooking for the party. I                          
U|                         promised I’d help.                                         
O|
C|                                   COACH                                            
U|                         I’d better go with them. See you at                        
U|                         the party.                                                 
N|               Coach goes after the boys, as they jump on their bikes and           
N|               cycle away up the track.                                             
O|
N|               Lek mounts his bike and pedals off in the opposite direction,        
N|               back into town.                                                      
O|
S|       2       EXT. MAIN ROAD - DAY                                     2           
O|
N|               Twelve boys and their coach, a column of bicycles, pedal up          
N|               the dirt track, shouting to each other as they go. The track         
N|               runs through rice fields where FARMERS are out tending their         
N|               crops.                                                               
O|
S|       3       EXT. THAM LUANG - CAVE ENTRANCE - DAY                    3           
O|
N|               The mountain is close now, looming overhead.                         
O|
N|               The boys dismount just before the mouth of the cave, and push        
N|               their bikes. They pass a small shrine where candles burn             
N|               before a statue of a reclining woman, a goddess, decorated           
N|               with garlands of flowers. They put their hands together and          
N|               make a quick token bow as they go by, and push their bikes on        
N|               to the cave. Prem forgets to pay his respects and turns back         
N|               for a hurried bow.                                                   
N|               Coach, bringing up the rear, also bows to the goddess, but he        
N|               does so more intently than the boys.                                 
O|
S|       4       INT. THAM LUANG - CAVE ENTRANCE - DAY                    4           
O|
N|               The boys wheel their bikes into the wide entrance to the dark        
N|               cave, and lean them against the long railing.                        
O|
O|
O|                 THIRTEEN LIVES | FULL PINK REVISIONS | 19.3.21 Pg 3.
O|
S|       5       INT. CHAMBER 1 - DAY                                     5           
N|               The boys head off in a laughing chattering band across the           
N|               immense cave entrance and into the wide tunnel on the far            
N|               side that leads to the inner chambers. They race through it,         
N|               their flashlight beams dancing on the rock walls.                    
O|
S|       6       INT. CHAMBER 3 - DAY                                     6           
O|
N|               The boys come out of the tunnel into a broad chamber, where a        
N|               little water has pooled onto its floor. They splash each             
N|               other as they race across, their flashlight beams reaching           
N|               ahead to the next tunnel. Some of the boys kick off their            
N|               shoes. Those still carrying rucksacks drop them off on the           
N|               wide rock shelf.                                                     
O|
S|       7       INT. STALACTITE TUNNEL - DAY                             7           
O|
N,G|               In the juddering flashlights we see Chai clambering down a           
N|               narrow sloping tunnel into a tight squeeze. He stops, looking        
N|               round, not sure if the boys are going further.                       
O|
N|               Arm shines his flashlight on Chai’s face.                            
O|
C|                                   ARM                                              
U|                         You scared?                                                
C|                                   CHAI                                             
U|                         No way! Let’s go!                                          
O|
N|               He pushes on into the tunnel. The others give a whoop and            
N|               follow.                                                              
O|
N,G|               THE CAMERA STAYS as the tunnel empties, and the sounds of the        
N|               boys fade to silence. Then all we hear is the trickle of the         
N|               water flowing in from the right-hand tunnel, and the water           
N|               seeping steadily down the walls to pool on the chamber floor.        
O|
D|       8       SCENE DELETED                                            8           
O|
S|       9       EXT. MAE SAI, THAILAND - NIGHT                           9           
O|
N|               Rain. Rain soaking down on the tropical forest round the             
N|               town. Rain making puddles on the paths between the houses.           
N|               Rain on the roofs and streaming down the narrow streets.             
O|
N|               A small motorbike comes put-putting through the rain. Its            
N,I|               rider is Chai’s 35-year-old mother BUAHOM, well-wrapped              
N|               against the rain. She weaves her way through the town,               
N|               splashing in and out of puddles.                                     
O|
O|
O|                 THIRTEEN LIVES | FULL PINK REVISIONS | 19.3.21 Pg 4.
O|
S|       10      INT. FAMILY HOUSE - MAE SAI - NIGHT                     10           
N|               Rain falling outside the windows. Buahom comes in, shaking           
N|               off the rain. She looks nervous, she’s not a regular part of         
N|               this group.                                                          
O|
C|                                   BUAHOM                                           
U|                         Am I late? The shop got really                             
U|                         busy.                                                      
O|
N,I|               The table is laid for a birthday party. MANOP, father of             
N,I|               birthday boy Prem, is on his phone. His wife WANNA, another          
N,I|               father, SOMBOON, and YOD and KAMPANG, father and mother of           
N,I|               Arm, are helping get the party ready. Wanna is putting               
N|               candles onto a birthday cake decorated with a frosting               
N|               version of SpongeBob SquarePants. For a moment no one’s              
N|               paying any attention to Buahom.                                      
C|                                   MANOP                                            
P|                             (to phone)                                             
U|                         Are they with you? Where are                               
U|                         they?...                                                   
O|
C|                                   BUAHOM                                           
U|                         What a great cake!                                         
O|
N|               Wanna now registers Buahom.                                          
C|                                   WANNA                                            
U|                         You’re Chai’s mum, right?                                  
O|
N|               Buahom nods.                                                         
O|
C|                                   BUAHOM                                           
U|                         I keep trying to get to watch the                          
U|                         games. There never seems to be                             
U|                         time.                                                      
O|
N|               Lek comes in from the kitchen carrying a plate of food.              
N|               Buahom looks round.                                                  
C|                                   BUAHOM                                           
U|                         Where are the boys?                                        
O|
C|                                   LEK                                              
U|                         They went to the cave.                                     
O|
C|                                   SOMBOON                                          
U|                         In this rain?                                              
O|
C|                                   LEK                                              
U|                         It wasn’t raining earlier.                                 
O|
O|
O|                 THIRTEEN LIVES | GOLDENROD REVISIONS | 25.9.21 Pg 5.
O|
C|                                   MANOP                                            
P|                             (to phone)                                             
U|                         Looks like they went to the cave...                        
U|                         Me too.                                                    
N|               He ends his phone call. Buahom looks at the rain streaming           
N|               down outside and starts to worry.                                    
O|
C|                                   BUAHOM                                           
U|                         Shouldn’t we drive over there and                          
U|                         get them? They’ll get soaked biking                        
U|                         back.                                                      
O|
C|                                   SOMBOON                                          
U|                         Serves them right! They’ve as much                         
U|                         sense as chickens.                                         
O|
S|       10A     EXT. MAE SAI - NIGHT                                   10A   *       
O|
N|               Rain streams down on the market area of town. In the cars,   *       
N|               Buahom, Lek, Somboon, and the other parents. The car radio is *      
N|               running a news bulletin.                                     *       
O|
C|                                   CAR RADIO                                *       
U|                         Heavy rain in Northern Thailand is                 *       
U|                         forecast to continue as the                        *       
U|                         moonsoon season starts -                           *       
N|               The people in the car react to the radio, speaking on top of *       
N|               the newsreader -                                             *       
O|
C|                                   BUAHOM                                   *       
U|                         Monsoon?                                           *       
O|
C|                                   CAR RADIO                                *       
U|                         Six weeks earlier than expected -                  *       
O|
C|                                   SOMBOON                                  *       
U|                         It can’t be the moonsoon.                          *       
C|                                   LEK                                      *       
U|                         That comes in July.                                *       
O|
C|                                   BUAHOM                                   *       
U|                         But that cave floods every year!                   *       
O|
C|                                   SOMBOON                                  *       
U|                         I’m sure they’re fine.                             *       
O|
O|
O|                 THIRTEEN LIVES | GOLDENROD REVISIONS | 25.9.21 Pg 5A.
