S|       11      EXT. THAM LUANG TRACK - NIGHT                           11           
N|               Rain streaming down as the day ends. Two cars jolt their way         
N|               up the track where the boys cycled. In the cars, Manop,              
N|               Wanna, Somboon, Yod, Kampang, Buahom and Lek.                        
O|
S|       12      EXT. THAM LUANG - CAVE ENTRANCE - NIGHT                 12           
O|
N|               Rain is already turning the track to mud as the cars pull up         
N|               by the Parks Building. Lights are on, and PARK RANGERS are           
N|               moving between the building and the entrance to the cave.            
O|
N|               The six parents and Lek get out of the cars, pulling hoods           
N|               over their head against the rain, and go to the cave.                
O|
S|       13      INT. THAM LUANG - CAVE ENTRANCE - NIGHT                 13           
O|
N|               The parents see the line of bikes leaning against the                
N|               railings. Buahom identifies Chai’s bike with a cry.                  
O|
C|                                   BUAHOM                                           
U|                         That’s Chai’s bike!                                        
O|
N|               Deeper inside the dark cave she sees men training the beams          
N|               of their flashlights on rising water. The sound of rushing           
N|               water everywhere.                                                    
N,I|               KITTIPONG SAISOR, a veteran park ranger, comes over to them.         
N|               He’s carrying a powerful flashlight.                                 
O|
C|                                   MANOP                                            
U|                         Where are the boys?                                        
O|
O|
O|                 THIRTEEN LIVES | FULL PINK REVISIONS | 19.3.21 Pg 6.
O|
C|                                   SAISOR                                           
U|                         We’ve been in as far as we could                           
U|                         go. The cave’s flooding. We’ve put                         
U|                         out an emergency call.                                     
C|                                   SOMBOON                                          
P|                             (to Manop)                                             
U|                         Let’s go in and get them.                                  
O|
N|               He and Manop head for the tunnel but Saisor blocks their way.        
O|
C|                                   SAISOR                                           
U|                         The cave’s closed! Look! It’s                              
U|                         flooding!                                                  
C|                                   BUAHOM                                           
U|                         How can the cave be closed? How are                        
U|                         they to come out?                                          
O|
N|               She starts to shout for her son -                                    
O|
C|                                   BUAHOM                                           
U|                         Chai! Chai! Can you hear me?                               
O|
S|       14      EXT. GOVERNOR’S HOUSE - CHIANG RAI - NIGHT              14           
N|               Rain falling. A car and driver stands waiting, engine                
N,I|               running, as GOVERNOR NARONGSAK comes out of his house,               
N,I|               pulling up his coat’s hood against the rain. His female              
N,I|               assistant PREEYA is by the car.                                      
O|
C|                                   NARONGSAK                                        
U|                         I’d just started my dinner.                                
O|
C|                                   PREEYA                                           
U|                         Sorry, Governor.                                           
O|
N|               The Governor gets into the back of the car. Preeya gets in           
N|               the front by the driver. The car pulls away.                         
O|
S|       15      INT/EXT. CAR - DRIVING - NIGHT                          15           
O|
C|                                   NARONGSAK                                        
U|                         Strictly speaking, none of this is                         
U|                         my responsibility now. You know                            
U|                         what my next job is?                                       
O|
C|                                   PREEYA                                           
U|                         No, sir.                                                   
O|
O|
O|                 THIRTEEN LIVES | FULL PINK REVISIONS | 19.3.21 Pg 7.
O|
C|                                   NARONGSAK                                        
U|                         Nor do I. The Minister hasn’t been                         
U|                         kind enough to tell me yet. So what                        
U|                         is this? Some kids stuck in a cave?                        
C|                                   PREEYA                                           
U|                         Yes, sir. A youth football team.                           
O|
C|                                   NARONGSAK                                        
U|                         Football team! They play football                          
U|                         in caves? Look at this rain! How                           
U|                         far is this cave?                                          
O|
C|                                   PREEYA                                           
U|                         About an hour and a half, sir.                             
N|               The Governor sighs.                                                  
O|
C|                                   NARONGSAK                                        
U|                         And no dinner.                                             
O|
S|       16      EXT. CAVE ENTRANCE - NIGHT                              16           
O|
N|               The mountain looms in the darkness beneath the night sky.            
N,G|               DOWN to see the headlights of cars and trucks sweeping               
N|               towards the cave. People hurrying back and forth in the rain-        
N|               drenched night.                                                      
N|               Two buses drive in. Out of the buses streams a platoon of            
N,I|               NAVY SEALS, led by their commander CAPTAIN ARNONT SUREEWONG,         
N,I|               40, slight in build, close-cropped hair, glasses: an                 
N,I|               intellectual-looking military man. As his men unpack their           
N|               diving gear the Governor’s car arrives. Narongsak and Preeya         
N|               get out. They see the Navy Seals getting ready to enter the          
N|               cave.                                                                
O|
C|                                   NARONGSAK                                        
U|                         Who called in the Navy?                                    
N|               He goes over to the Seals and speaks to Captain Arnont.              
O|
C|                                   NARONGSAK                                        
U|                         I’m the Governor of the province.                          
U|                         You are?                                                   
O|
C|                                   CAPTAIN ARNONT                                   
U|                         Captain Arnont Sureewong, sir. Navy                        
U|                         Seals.                                                     
O|
N|               His attention is on his men, and he barely glances at the            
N|               Governor.                                                            
O|
O|
O|                 THIRTEEN LIVES | FULL PINK REVISIONS | 19.3.21 Pg 8.
O|
C|                                   NARONGSAK                                        
U|                         Brief me, please.                                          
C|                                   CAPTAIN ARNONT                                   
U|                         The cave is flooded. My men will                           
U|                         enter with breathing apparatus.                            
U|                         It’s all under control.                                    
O|
N,I|               Preeya joins the Governor with a lean Englishman who’s just          
N,I|               arrived, VERN UNSWORTH, 60.                                          
O|
C|                                   PREEYA                                           
U|                         This man lives near by, sir. He                            
U|                         knows the cave.                                            
C|                                   VERN UNSWORTH                                    
U|                         I’ve mapped it. All of it.                                 
O|
N|               He’s pulling out a hand-drawn map. The Governor studies it by        
N|               the light of his phone.                                              
O|
C|                                   VERN UNSWORTH                                    
U|                         I’ve never been in when it’s                               
U|                         flooded - that’s a whole different                         
U|                         game. You have to be a bit -                               
O|
N|               He makes a gesture meaning ‘crazy’.                                  
C|                                   VERN UNSWORTH                                    
U|                         There’s some pretty tight corners                          
U|                         in there, real squeeze. But there’s                        
U|                         some big chambers too. The boys                            
U|                         should be okay, so long as we get                          
U|                         them out soon.                                             
O|
N|               Captain Arnont is now also looking at Vern’s map.                    
O|
C|                                   CAPTAIN ARNONT                                   
U|                         Let me show this to my men.                                
N|               Narongsak nods. Vern and Captain Arnont go into a huddle over        
N|               the map with the Navy Seals. The Governor finds himself              
N|               effectively left out as the professionals get into the               
N|               details.                                                             
O|
C|                                   PREEYA                                           
U|                         Maybe I could find you something to                        
U|                         eat, sir.                                                  
O|
C|                                   NARONGSAK                                        
U|                         That would be kind. This could be a                        
U|                         long night.                                                
O|
O|
