S|       17      INT. CAVE ENTRANCE - NIGHT                              17           
N|               Buahom and the other parents look on as a powerful light is          
N|               dragged into the cave. It comes on, dazzling everyone. Its           
N,G|               light illuminates the great space so that we see it clearly          
N,M|               for the first time. From the railing where the parents stand         
N|               and the bikes are parked a rock face slopes steeply down to          
N|               an immense void, bigger than a football arena, with                  
N|               stalactites stabbing down from the high rock roof like               
N|               monster’s teeth. At the far end a lake has formed, into which        
N|               water is flowing from a wide rock tunnel. The light gleams on        
N|               the water, bouncing patterns onto the tunnel roof.                   
O|
N|               The team of Navy Seals now enter the cave, ready to dive,            
N,I|               wearing head-torches. Their leader, LIEUTENANT KIET, a super-        
N,I|               fit 25-year-old, leads them across the wide entrance. As they        
N|               reach the tunnel he pulls out a phone, holds it up for a             
N,I|               group selfie. His group includes a medic, DR KARN, and two           
N,I|               young eager Seals, JAY and PICHAI.                                   
C|                                   KIET                                             
U|                         Navy Seals! We don’t go home till                          
U|                         we’ve got the kids! Hooyah!                                
O|
N|               His comrades punch the air and echo their trademark cry.             
O|
C|                                   NAVY SEALS                                       
U|                         Hooyah!                                                    
O|
S|       18      INT. CHAMBER 1 - NIGHT                                  18           
O|
Y|               DAY 2 - Sunday June 24 (midnight)                                    
O|
N|               The Seals splash through shallow water down the wide tunnel.         
N|               The terrain rises and falls, and is strewn with boulders.            
N|               Their head-torches throw beams of light onto the craggy roof         
N|               and walls. The sound of gushing water fills the air.                 
O|
S|       18A     INT. U-BEND - NIGHT                                    18A           
O|
N|               The Navy Seals stride across U-Bend to the point where the           
N|               next tunnel is almost completely filled with water. Here the         
N|               diving begins.                                                       
O|
N|               Kiet looks round his men, fixes his mask. They all follow            
N|               suit. He gives them a thumbs-up, and submerges himself under         
N|               the murky water. One by one his men follow him, and they’re          
N|               gone.                                                                
O|
O|
O|                 THIRTEEN LIVES | FULL PINK REVISIONS | 19.3.21 Pg 10.
O|
S|       19      EXT. MOUNTAIN - NIGHT                                   19           
N|               The rain falls ceaselessly. Lightning lights up the long low         
N|               mountain.                                                            
O|
S|       20      EXT. THAM LUANG - BASECAMP - NIGHT                      20           
O|
N|               More and more cars arriving. A local TV news crew is setting         
N|               up camera and lights.                                                
O|
N|               The huddle of parents stands by the cave entrance, patiently         
N|               waiting for the Navy Seals to return with their boys. They’re        
N|               anxious, but still able to exchange chatter and even some            
N|               nervy laughter. Captain Arnont waits, staring towards the            
N|               cave.                                                                
O|
S|       21      EXT. THAM LUANG - BASECAMP - LATER - NIGHT              21           
O|
N|               Governor Narongsak speaking to a TV news crew in the rain.           
N|               He’s keen to communicate his confidence that everything’s            
N|               under control.                                                       
O|
C|                                   NARONGSAK                                        
U|                         It’s a deep cave, several                                  
U|                         kilometers long. It’s got some                             
U|                         tricky narrow passages. If the boys                        
U|                         have gone a long way in, it could                          
U|                         be a few more hours. I have every                          
U|                         confidence in the Navy Seals. They                         
U|                         know what they’re doing.                                   
O|
S|       22      INT. CAVE ENTRANCE - NIGHT                              22           
O|
N|               Flickers of light from deep in the tunnel. The lights grow           
N|               brighter.                                                            
O|
N,G|               Then they appear, moving slowly, exhausted and in pain: Kiet         
N|               and his team of Navy Seals wading their way through the water        
N|               back towards the cave mouth. One of the Seals is being               
N|               supported by comrades. Another has a cut on his brow that’s          
N|               bleeding.                                                            
N|               Captain Arnont, Governor Narongsak and Preeya - a huddle of          
N|               parents, Buahom a little apart, by the railing - all staring         
N|               in shock.                                                            
O|
N|               The Navy Seals come to a stop and pull off their masks, and          
N|               meet the stunned gaze of all the people waiting in the cave.         
N|               Kiet shakes his head.                                                
O|
O|
O|                 THIRTEEN LIVES | FULL PINK REVISIONS | 19.3.21 Pg 11.
O|
N|               Buahom gives a gasping sob. Governor Narongsak and Captain           
N|               Arnont share a look: what now?                                       
O|
S|       23      INT. RICK STANTON’S HOUSE - COVENTRY, ENGLAND - DAY     23           
O|
Y|               DAY 3 - Monday June 25                                               
O|
N,I|               Lean, crop-headed RICK STANTON, 57, is bent over a worktop           
N|               covered in tools, constructing a home-made re-breather, part         
N|               of his diving kit. All round him the clutter of a man who            
N|               lives alone, his life given over to his hobbies, which are           
N|               cave diving and kayaking. Bottles of oxygen, diving                  
N|               apparatus, kayaks under repair, compete for space with a             
N|               couch, a TV, and the remains of takeaway meals.                      
N|               The phone buzzes. Without stopping what he’s doing Rick taps         
N|               the call onto speaker.                                               
O|
C|                                   RICK STANTON                                     
U|                         Yeah. John.                                                
O|
C,E|                                   JOHN VOLANTHEN’S PHONE VOICE                     
U|                         You following what’s happening in                          
U|                         Thailand?                                                  
O|
C|                                   RICK STANTON                                     
U|                         Why would I?                                               
C,E|                                   JOHN VOLANTHEN’S PHONE VOICE                     
U|                         Some kids stuck in a cave.                                 
O|
C|                                   RICK STANTON                                     
U|                         How’d they get themselves in there?                        
O|
C,E|                                   JOHN VOLANTHEN’S PHONE VOICE                     
U|                         How do I know?                                             
O|
C|                                   RICK STANTON                                     
U|                         If they walked in, they can walk                           
U|                         out.                                                       
O|
S|       24      INT. JOHN VOLANTHEN’S HOUSE - LONG ASHTON, ENGLAND - DAY 24          
O|
N|               COMPUTER SCREEN - BBC News Asia: Tham Luang - Twelve members         
N|               of a youth soccer team and their coach reported missing in a         
N|               cave in northern Thailand.                                           
O|
