O|
N,G|               DIVERS POV - The blur of rock walls as they loom out of the          
N|               murk. Rapid turns to avoid contact. Bare hands feeling their         
N,G|               way. The light of a head-torch revealing high crags and              
N,G|               sudden drops into nothing. Glimpses of hosepipes clustered on        
N|               the rock floor. Short stretches of rope fixed to the side,           
N,G|               then ending. All seen through a constantly surging churn of          
N|               tea-colored water that carries debris along with it.                 
N|               They skillfully negotiate a pinch-point. The sound of the            
N|               divers’ steady breathing. The trail of bubbles from their            
N|               masks.                                                               
O|
